IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei7-related-nouns`
IMPORT `ei7-related-2003-2010`

-- Tests of ei7-related-2003-2010. Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the related provision
-- named above it; none is copied from the encoding's output. Dates that an amending Act leaves to "the day on which
-- this Act comes into force" or "receives royal assent" are not in the deposited text, so the days used for them
-- below are chosen to test the boundary and are not the real days.

§ `2003, c. 15, s. 25(1)`

-- (a) a benefit period beginning on January 4, 2004 (a Sunday): every week is covered.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2004 1 4), (YMD 2004 12 31)) (YMD 2004 1 4)
-- (a) the day before: not (a); the benefit period has not ended before January 4, 2004, so (b) covers only weeks that begin on or after that day.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2004 1 3), (YMD 2005 1 1)) (YMD 2004 1 4)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2004 1 3), (YMD 2005 1 1)) (YMD 2003 12 28))
-- (b) a benefit period whose last day is January 4, 2004 has not ended before that day.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2003 6 1), (YMD 2004 1 4)) (YMD 2004 1 4)
-- a benefit period whose last day is January 3, 2004 ended before that day: neither paragraph.
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2003 6 1), (YMD 2004 1 3)) (YMD 2004 1 4))
-- a benefit period that began long before and ended long before.
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2003 c. 15 s. 25(1) sections 15 to 20 and 22 apply to the week of benefits` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2002 1 6), (YMD 2002 12 28)) (YMD 2002 6 2))

§ `2005, c. 34, s. 56`

#ASSERT `Act RP 2005 c. 34 s. 56 the validity of a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections 127 and 128` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Act RP 2005 c. 34 s. 56 the validity of a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections 127 and 128` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not made under sections 127 or 128, or not by the Ministers named: the saving says nothing.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2005 c. 34 s. 56 the validity of a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections 127 and 128` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act RP 2005 c. 34 s. 56 the validity of a disclosure or agreement made under the repealed sections 127 and 128` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2008, c. 28, s. 39(3), (4)`

#ASSERT `Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39(3) subsection (1) applies to the remittance` TRUE (YMD 2008 2 26)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39(3) subsection (1) applies to the remittance` TRUE (YMD 2008 2 25))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39(3) subsection (1) applies to the remittance` FALSE (YMD 2008 3 31))
#ASSERT `Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39(4) subsection (2) applies to the payment or remittance` (YMD 2008 2 26)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2008 c. 28 s. 39(4) subsection (2) applies to the payment or remittance` (YMD 2008 2 25))

§ `2009, c. 2, s. 226(2)`

-- March 12, 2009 was a Thursday: the first Sunday before is March 8 and the second March 1.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 12) EQUALS YMD 2009 3 1
-- A Monday: the first Sunday before is the day before.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 9) EQUALS YMD 2009 3 1
-- A Sunday: that Sunday is not "before" the day, so the first is the Sunday a week earlier and the second a week before that.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the second Sunday before the day on which the Act receives royal assent` (YMD 2009 3 8) EQUALS YMD 2009 2 22
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the maximum number of weeks is determined under Schedule I as enacted by subsection 224(1)` TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 9 1), (YMD 2009 3 1)) (YMD 2009 3 12)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the maximum number of weeks is determined under Schedule I as enacted by subsection 224(1)` TRUE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 9 1), (YMD 2009 2 28)) (YMD 2009 3 12))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 226(2) the maximum number of weeks is determined under Schedule I as enacted by subsection 224(1)` FALSE (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 9 1), (YMD 2009 12 31)) (YMD 2009 3 12))

§ `2009, c. 2, ss. 227 and 228`

#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 227 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.1` 2002 EQUALS JUST (2.2%)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 227 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.1` 2003 EQUALS JUST (2.1%)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 227 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.1` 2001 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 227 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.1` 2004 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 228 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.3` 2005 EQUALS JUST (1.95%)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 228 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.3` 2004 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 228 the premium rate for the year deemed by section 66.3` 2006 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2009, c. 2, s. 229`

#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 subsection 224(1) applies to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (YMD 2009 12 31)
-- "does not begin after September 11, 2010": the day itself is inside, the next day is outside.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 subsection 224(1) applies to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 9 11), (YMD 2011 9 10)) (YMD 2009 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 subsection 224(1) applies to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 9 12), (YMD 2011 9 11)) (YMD 2009 12 31))
-- "has not ended before the day": a benefit period whose last day is the day itself has not ended before it.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 subsection 224(1) applies to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 1 4), (YMD 2009 12 31)) (YMD 2009 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 2 s. 229 subsection 224(1) applies to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2009 1 4), (YMD 2009 12 30)) (YMD 2009 12 31))

§ `2009, c. 30, s. 7`

#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 subsection 55(10) of the Regulations is deemed to read as set out in this section` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 subsection 55(10) of the Regulations is deemed to read as set out in this section` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 subsection 55(10) of the Regulations is deemed to read as set out in this section` FALSE FALSE)
-- the cap is 50, unless the maximum under section 225 is 50 or more, when it is that maximum.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the most weeks of benefits that may be paid in total when weeks are combined` 49 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the most weeks of benefits that may be paid in total when weeks are combined` 50 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the most weeks of benefits that may be paid in total when weeks are combined` 52 EQUALS 52
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the most weeks of benefits that may be paid in total when weeks are combined` 0 EQUALS 50
-- gate, a claimant outside Canada, 60 weeks entitled, (7) maximum 45, section 225 maximum 52: the lesser of 60, 45 and 52.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 60 45 52 EQUALS JUST 45
-- 30 weeks entitled is the least.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 30 45 52 EQUALS JUST 30
-- the section 225 maximum of 55 is the least of 60, 70 and 55.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 60 70 55 EQUALS JUST 55
-- the section 225 maximum of 40 is under 50, so the cap is 50: the least of 60, 70 and 50.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 60 70 40 EQUALS JUST 50
-- a claimant referred to in subsection (8) who is in Canada.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 60 70 40 EQUALS JUST 50
-- neither outside Canada nor referred to in (8): the deemed text gives no power to combine.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60 70 40 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the benefit period was extended under 10(13): the deemed text does not apply.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 60 70 40 EQUALS NOTHING
-- none of sections 3 to 6 applies.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 30 s. 7 the total number of weeks of benefits that the claimant may combine` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 60 70 40 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2009, c. 33, ss. 18 to 20`

-- royal assent July 1, 2009 and section 16 in force January 1, 2010 (illustrative days).
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into on the day` (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2010 1 1)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into on the day` (YMD 2010 1 1) (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2010 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into on the day` (YMD 2009 6 30) (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2010 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 an agreement referred to in subsection 152.02(1) may be entered into on the day` (YMD 2010 1 2) (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2010 1 1))
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 the day on which the agreement is deemed to have been entered into` (YMD 2009 9 15) (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2010 1 1)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 the day on which the agreement is deemed to have been entered into` (YMD 2010 1 1) (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2010 1 1)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 18 the day on which the agreement is deemed to have been entered into` (YMD 2010 3 1) (YMD 2009 7 1) (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 19, royal assent before January 1, 2010: the period is January 1 to April 1, 2010.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` (YMD 2011 1 1) (YMD 2010 1 1) (YMD 2009 12 1)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` (YMD 2011 1 1) (YMD 2010 4 1) (YMD 2009 12 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` (YMD 2011 1 1) (YMD 2009 12 31) (YMD 2009 12 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` (YMD 2011 1 1) (YMD 2010 4 2) (YMD 2009 12 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` (YMD 2010 12 31) (YMD 2010 2 1) (YMD 2009 12 1))
-- royal assent on February 15, 2010 is later than January 1, 2010: the period begins on February 15.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` (YMD 2011 1 1) (YMD 2010 2 15) (YMD 2010 2 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 19 a benefit period under Part VII.1 may begin on or after January 1, 2011` (YMD 2011 1 1) (YMD 2010 2 14) (YMD 2010 2 15))
-- section 20.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 20 the day on which the violation is deemed to have been accumulated under section 152.07` TRUE (YMD 2009 8 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2009 8 3)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2009 c. 33 s. 20 the day on which the violation is deemed to have been accumulated under section 152.07` FALSE (YMD 2009 8 3) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `2010, c. 9, s. 4`

-- the day the 2010 Act comes into force is taken as June 1, 2010 (illustrative). 728 days before it is June 3, 2008.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the period began less than 104 weeks before the day on which the Act comes into force` (YMD 2008 6 4) (YMD 2010 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the period began less than 104 weeks before the day on which the Act comes into force` (YMD 2008 6 3) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the period began less than 104 weeks before the day on which the Act comes into force` (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the period began less than 104 weeks before the day on which the Act comes into force` (YMD 2010 6 1) (YMD 2010 6 1))
-- 104 weeks from Friday January 1, 2010, the first day included, end on Wednesday December 29, 2011.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the last day of a period extended to 104 weeks` (YMD 2010 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2011 12 29
-- subsection (1)(a): the period under 23(2) has not ended before the day.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(1) sections 2 and 3 apply to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) FALSE (YMD 2010 1 1) (YMD 2010 6 1)
-- (1)(b): the period ended before the day, leave was deferred within it, and the deferral has not ended before the day.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(1) sections 2 and 3 apply to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 6 1) (YMD 2010 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(1) sections 2 and 3 apply to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(1) sections 2 and 3 apply to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) FALSE (YMD 2010 6 1) (YMD 2010 6 1))
-- (1): the benefit period began 104 weeks or more before the day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(1) sections 2 and 3 apply to the claimant` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 6 3), (YMD 2010 6 30)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 6 3), (YMD 2010 6 30)) FALSE (YMD 2010 6 1) (YMD 2010 6 1))
-- subsection (2): leave deferred within the period; deferral ended before the day; benefit period not ended; the 23(2) period ended before the day.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(2) section 2 applies and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) is extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(2) section 2 applies and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) is extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 6 1) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(2) section 2 applies and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) is extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(2) section 2 applies and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) is extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 6 1)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(2) section 2 applies and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) is extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 12 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) FALSE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
-- subsection (3): the benefit period and the 23(2) period each began less than 104 weeks before the day and both ended before it.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(3) the benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) are each extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(3) the benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) are each extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 6 1)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(3) the benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) are each extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 6 1)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(3) the benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) are each extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2008 6 3), (YMD 2010 5 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(3) the benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) are each extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) FALSE (YMD 2010 5 31) (YMD 2010 6 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4(3) the benefit period and the period referred to in subsection 23(2) are each extended to 104 weeks` (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) (`Period of days` OF (YMD 2010 1 1), (YMD 2010 5 31)) TRUE (YMD 2010 6 1) (YMD 2010 6 1))
-- the extended last day.
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the last day of the period as extended to 104 weeks` (YMD 2010 1 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2011 12 29)
#ASSERT `Act RP 2010 c. 9 s. 4 the last day of the period as extended to 104 weeks` (YMD 2010 1 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
